\title{Architecture-conditioned potential and computation}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{chapter}

\p{This chapter refines the [evaluation framework](ftip-005C) for claims
that depend on architecture, optimization geometry or a systems
implementation. It begins with the decoder-only Transformer, then maps
mechanism families to capability bottlenecks before introducing
architecture-indexed frontiers and matched-compute comparisons. It also
studies how an optimizer can depend on the representation of its parameters.}

\p{The reference architecture specifies how token probabilities are
computed; it does not replace the shared task and evaluation interfaces. The
[mechanism-family map](ftip-00OQ) asks which bottleneck a design changes and
what evidence would demonstrate that change; it does not rank model families.
Readers whose question does not depend on an architecture or optimizer can
continue directly to [conceptual discovery](ftip-00MH). Changes to retained
context and rollout computation are treated with
[agent state](ftip-00DA).}

